Does this game seem to good to be true?
Absolutely! For it is designed around the concept of giving with one hand and subtly taking with the other.
The hand that gives:
- All guns and equipment can be obtained through farming or ingame transactions from a virtual store without real money;
- Multiplayer and coop are above average in a sense that the overall design of the guns, levels and AI doesnt make you feel like you the need to pay real money in order to enjoy the game;
- The gunplay is excellent even though the guns are somewhat inaccurate;
- The AI is capable and it will mostly (MOSTLY) be the reason why you die in coop and not because of ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥t like an overpowered AI opponent in a corridor or a corner;
- For every obstacle in the game there is a mechanic that you do not have to pay for to surpass it;
The hand that takes:
(Because it is a free to play and most companies refuse to accept that the business model of the game LOADOUT actually works financially for both the consumers and the devs)
- Each new daily coop level is just the same but with enemies in different positions.
- Strong cooperation between players is essential to win high level matches of both pvp or pve in nature. Cooperation is impossible since the game is built around making it so.
- Once you get medium to high level gear, fixing it after a match costs more than you can earn at the end of it forcing you to spend REAL money in order to pay the repair bills.
- You only get money after wining a match, your equipment however needs to be repaired still (even if you leave the match midgame).
Honestly I only play this game because I do not posses a decent computer to run Planetside 2 above 20 fps. And also because I got tired of all the other games I have.
